course: dictionary
lesson: 174
title: Agouti: an animal and a colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have two meanings. The dictionary gives agouti as an animal and as a fur colour pattern. Context tells you which one an author means. «Agoutis open hard Brazil nut pods and bury spare seeds, and the forgotten seeds grow into new Brazil nut trees.» Agoutis are the subject, and they open pods and bury seeds, so here agouti means the animal.
explain: Check by swapping the meaning into the sentence. Could a fur pattern open pods and bury seeds? No, so the animal meaning fits. Now try a different sentence: «The wild mouse had a grey agouti coat with bands of light and dark.» A coat can have a pattern, so this time agouti means the fur colour.
explain: Always ask: which meaning makes sense here? Look at the words around the word, and try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: A rodent is a small animal with sharp front teeth for gnawing.
fact: «Agouti» means a rodent of Central and South America, with long legs, like a large guinea pig, that eats fruit and nuts.
fact: «Agouti» also means a fur colour pattern where each hair has bands of light and dark.
fact: Wild rabbits and mice often have the agouti fur pattern.
fact: Agoutis help Brazil nut trees grow: the seeds they bury and forget can sprout into new trees.
exercise: «Agoutis open hard Brazil nut pods and bury spare seeds.» In this sentence, what is an agouti? | *A rodent with long legs | A kind of nut | A type of tree | A fur colour
exercise: An agouti looks most like which animal? | A bird | A cat | A fish | *A large guinea pig
exercise: A wild rabbit has hairs with bands of light and dark. What is this fur pattern called? | Rodent | Terrier | *Agouti | Pod
test: «Agoutis bury spare seeds, and the forgotten seeds grow into new trees.» Why do the forgotten seeds matter? | They turn into fruit | They become guinea pigs | *They grow into new Brazil nut trees | They make the hard pod heavier
test: «The wild mouse had an agouti coat.» What does agouti mean in this sentence? | A rodent | A kind of tree | A type of nut | *A fur pattern of light and dark bands
exam: Jade reads «The agouti's coat had bands of light and dark.» Which meaning fits, and why? | The tree, because trees have bark with bands | *The fur pattern, because the sentence describes a coat with bands | The animal, because it is a rodent with long legs | The nut, because nuts are often brown
